ROOT_STATEMENT = "Root of the compiler optimization causation world: how syntax, intermediate representations, dependence proofs, semantic permissions, runtime guards and execution evidence enable or constrain program transformations."
LIMITATIONS = [
    "All prose is original. Source-language undefined behavior, LLVM poison, LLVM undef, a verifier error and a runtime exception are different states.",
    "A legal transformation preserves the required defined observable behavior under its stated hypotheses. It is neither a guarantee of speedup nor a claim that every compiler version implements that transformation.",
    "Parsing examples use a declared expression grammar; arithmetic and loop examples state their integer width, floating-point rules, memory bounds and alias assumptions.",
    "Runtime feedback supports heuristic choices. A speculation requires its own valid guard or dependency mechanism and a state-reconstruction path; a hot observation alone is not a correctness proof.",
    "Debug information, optimization level, assertions, sanitizers and floating-point permission flags are separate configuration dimensions. No universal debug-versus-release macro configuration is inferred.",
]

